### NOT DONE — the live dev run and the two DB-level seeds

The work order asks for the census to be RUN on dev (expected 35 works, 8 registers), with a
not-admitted work seeded into the database to watch it STOP, and a forbidden-provenance work
made reachable to watch it appear in §2. None of that was done.

This tree has no dev credentials: no .env.local (root or web/), no DATABASE_URL, no
NEON_API_KEY. scripts/publish-flip-census.mts therefore has never been executed — not once,
against anything. Two consequences worth stating plainly rather than leaving implied:

  1. Its SQL is UNRUN. The queries in §1–§4 have not been parsed by a Postgres server, so a
     syntax error, a wrong column name, or a type mismatch would not have been caught here.
     The 15 green tests exercise the VERDICT logic and the runner's import discipline; they
     do not execute a single one of its statements.
  2. The "35 works, 8 registers" figure is unverified by me and is not repeated as fact
     anywhere in this branch.

What IS discharged: both STOP rules, driven red and back through real product code, plus the
static guarantee that the runner imports LEGAL_CORPUS_FILTER / SERVED_PROSE_WORKS /
SERVED_LANE_WORKS rather than restating them, and that it refuses production outright.

